mma":"சென்ற","gloss":"who went"}],"gloss":"who went","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"இரவலர்","parts":[{"text":"இரவலர்","lemma":"இரவலர்","gloss":"suppliants"}],"gloss":"suppliants"},{"surface":"சுட்டி","parts":[{"text":"சுட்டு","lemma":"சுட்டு","gloss":"point out/aim at"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"இ","gloss":"verbal participle suffix"}],"gloss":"seeking"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தொடுத்துணக்","parts":[{"text":"தொடுத்துணக்","lemma":"தொடுத்துணக்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கிடப்பினும்","parts":[{"text":"கிடப்பினும்","lemma":"கிடப்பினும்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கிடக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"கிடக்கும்","lemma":"கிடக்கும்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அஃதான்று","parts":[{"text":"அஃதான்று","lemma":"அஃதான்று","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"நிறை","parts":[{"text":"நிறை","lemma":"நிறை","gloss":"abundance"}],"gloss":"abundant"},{"surface":"அருந்","parts":[{"text":"அரு","lemma":"அருமை","gloss":"rare/difficult"},{"text":"ந்","lemma":"ந்","gloss":"sandhi"}],"gloss":"formidable"},{"surface":"தானை","parts":[{"text":"தானை","lemma":"தானை","gloss":"army"}],"gloss":"army"},{"surface":"வேந்தரை","parts":[{"text":"வேந்தர்","lemma":"வேந்தன்","gloss":"king"},{"text":"ஐ","lemma":"ஐ","gloss":"accusative case marker"}],"gloss":"kings"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"திறை","parts":[{"text":"திறை","lemma":"திறை","gloss":"tribute"}],"gloss":"tribute"},{"surface":"கொண்டு","parts":[{"text":"கொண்டு","lemma":"கொண்டு","gloss":"having taken"}],"gloss":"having taken","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பெயர்க்கும்","parts":[{"text":"பெயர்","lemma":"பெயர்","gloss":"move/remove"},{"text":"க்கு","lemma":"க்கு","gloss":"formative/transitivizer"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"making them retreat"},{"surface":"செம்மலும்","parts":[{"text":"செம்மல்","lemma":"செம்மல்","gloss":"greatness/pride"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"the pride also"},{"surface":"உடைத்தே","parts":[{"text":"உடைத்து","lemma":"உடைத்து","gloss":"it possesses"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"indeed it possesses"}]}],"literal":"One good thing possessing others' hills always, / Two good things indeed possesses Koṇ's great forest. / Desiring and going suppliants pointing at, / to string and eat even if it lies, it will lie; besides that, / abundant rare army kings, / taking tribute, making them retreat, the pride also indeed it possesses.","translation":"The hills of other kings always have but one good thing. But the great forest of Koṇ has two good things! For the suppliants who come seeking him with desire, there is food lying ready to be strung and eaten. Besides that, it also possesses the pride of making kings with vast, formidable armies pay tribute and retreat.","modern":"மற்றவர்களுடைய மலைகள் எப்போதும் ஒரு நன்மையையே கொண்டிருக்கின்றன. ஆனால், கொண்கானங் கிழானின் பெரிய காடு இரண்டு நன்மைகளைக் கொண்டிருக்கிறது. தன்னை விரும்பி வந்த இரவலர்களைக் கருதி, அவர்கள் தொடுத்து உண்ணும் வகையில் உணவு எப்போதும் தயாராகக் கிடக்கும்; அதுமட்டுமல்லாமல், நிறைந்த வலிமையான படைகளைக் கொண்ட பகை வேந்தர்களிடம் திறை பெற்று அவர்களைத் திருப்பி அனுப்பும் பெருமையையும் அது பெற்றுள்ளது.","explanation":"The poet Mōcikīraṉār sings in praise of the chieftain Koṇkāṉaṅ kiḻāṉ, highlighting his extraordinary generosity and military prowess. He contrasts the hills of other rulers, which possess only one virtue, with the great forest of Koṇ, which possesses two. The first virtue is the abundance of food, which lies ready for visiting suppliants to string together and eat. The second virtue is the political power to extract tribute from mighty kings with vast armies and make them retreat. This poem belongs to the pāṭāṇ tiṇai, which focuses on praising a patron's virtues, strength, and generosity. Key words like iravalar (suppliants) and tiṟai (tribute) emphasize the dual themes of boundless charity and supreme sovereignty.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.8],[0.8,1.1],[1.1,1.3],[1.3,1.5],[1.5,2.1],[2.1,3.12],[3.12,3.3],[3.3,3.9],[3.9,4.4],[4.4,5.6],[5.67,5.9],[5.9,6.2],[6.28,6.35],[6.42,7.47],[7.8,8.3],[8.3,8.4],[8.4,9.3],[9.3,10.2],[10.2,10.7],[10.7,11.2],[11.2,12.4],[12.4,12.9],[12.9,13.4],[13.4,13.5]],"female":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.2],[1.2,1.5],[1.5,1.8],[1.8,2.5],[2.5,3.82],[3.82,4.0],[4.0,4.8],[4.8,5.4],[5.7,6.3],[6.3,6.9],[6.9,7.8],[7.85,7.9],[7.9,8.8],[9.1,9.5],[9.5,9.7],[9.7,10.5],[10.5,12.0],[12.0,12.3],[12.4,13.1],[13.1,14.1],[14.1,14.7],[14.7,15.2],[15.2,15.3]]},"sync":[[["ஒன்று","one thing"],["நன்கு","goodness"]],[["நன்கு","goodness"],["உடைய","possessing"]],[["பிறர்","of others"]],[["குன்றம்","hill"]],[["என்றும்","always"]],[["இரண்டு","two things"],["நன்கு","goodness"]],[["நன்கு","goodness"],["உடைத்தே","indeed it possesses"]],[["கொண்பெருங்","Koṇ's great"]],[["கானம்","forest"]],[["நச்சி","having desired"]],[["சென்ற","who went"]],[["இரவலர்","suppliants"],["சுட்டி","seeking"]],[["சுட்டி","seeking"]],[["தொடுத்துணக்",""]],[["கிடப்பினும்",""]],[["கிடக்கும்",""]],[["அஃதான்று",""]],[["நிறை","abundant"],["அருந்","formidable"]],[["தானை","army"]],[["வேந்தரை","kings"]],[["திறை","tribute"],["கொண்டு","having taken"]],[["பெயர்க்கும்","making them retreat"]],[["செம்மலும்","the pride also"]],[["உடைத்தே","indeed it possesses"]]]}